{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And I will bless her.</b> And what is the blessing? That she returned to her youth, as is said ״הָיְתָה לִּי עֶדְנָה״ (Genesis 18)." "<b>And I will bless her.</b> With fullness of breasts, when she had need of that on the day of Isaac's feast — for they would murmur about them that they had brought a foundling from the market and would say 'our son is he,' and each woman brought her son with her, but she who had nursed did not bring — and she nursed them all; as is said ״הֵינִיקָה בָנִים שָׂרָה״, Bereshit Rabbah, hinting at a portion."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:04.165899545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}